# p_alloc_s2: diagnostic, not a step. s2's lever set with the glibc allocator pinned.
#
# hypothesis from SHAFT-CPU: host peak from s4 on takes one of two values ~382 MB apart (dynamic mmap
#            threshold: freeing a large mmap'd block raises it, later same-size requests come from
#            the arena). Pinning the tunables cut the replicate spread 9.35% -> 0.574%.
# here       same stack (CrypTen, int64 host shares). Party peaks (kB):
#              s0_default    2,956,388  2,945,664 | 2,923,028  2,929,724 | 3,361,452  2,945,240
#              s1_limb_loop  2,876,448  2,951,704 | 2,942,436  3,333,668 | 2,939,436  2,955,272
#            ten at 2.88 to 2.96 M, two at 3.33 to 3.36 M: bimodal, gap ~420 MB.
# explains   published host spreads 16.79% (s0), 14.28% (s1); s3_plaintext_free (972 MB) and
#            s3_plaintext_free_early (433 MB) moved the peak 0.09%. Alternative ("poller misses a
#            spike") weakened: polled_vs_hwm_pct ~0.
# status     not a step: allocator settings target anon: (p_alloc_probe, SHAFT-CPU); whether
#            the runtime-knob exception applies is open.
SHAFT_LIMB_LOOP=1
SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=1 MALLOC_TRIM_THRESHOLD_=0 MALLOC_MMAP_THRESHOLD_=131072"
